  "crew": [
    {
      "name": "Thomas Huyghues Despointes",
      "avatar": "/media/media::image::c::7579668770::vessel::34a65990-fca3-11ee-ad26-6f560b16d431::assets::220f3df0-ceb6-11f1-a1da-bd33f7faec83/{imageVariant}",
      "role": "Captain",
      "bio": "Sail and Work Experience\n\nThomas is an experienced yacht captain with an extensive background in private yachting, charter operations, regattas, and yacht management. Most recently, he captained the 75-foot Sangermani sailing yacht ELSTIR in the Mediterranean, overseeing private operations and racing activities. Previously, he served as captain aboard the 80-foot Sunreef SEACLUSION in the Caribbean and the 80-foot Vismara LUCE GUIDA, cruising between the Mediterranean and Caribbean.\n\nHis career also includes captaining the 62-foot Lagoon VACOA and the day-charter catamaran ECOLORATO, accommodating up to 110 passengers. He has worked as a freelance captain on yachts ranging from 50 to 110 feet and served as First Mate and Chief Engineer aboard SMART SPIRIT. In addition, Thomas spent several years as a surf boat pilot for BOURBON OFF SHORE SURF in Central Africa. Earlier in his career, he worked as a yacht broker for A&C YACHT BROKER, specialising in yacht sales, preparation, and deliveries. His experience includes crew management, yacht maintenance, flag-state compliance, and regatta preparation across the Mediterranean, Caribbean, USA, and UK.\n\nJob Description\n\nThomas is responsible for the overall operation, navigation, safety, and management of the yacht, its crew, and guests. He ensures the vessel operates safely and efficiently while maintaining compliance with flag-state regulations, maritime laws, and onboard safety procedures. He oversees crew recruitment, training, and daily operations, encouraging teamwork and maintaining high standards of service. His responsibilities also include yacht maintenance, technical management, financial and administrative oversight, and the planning and execution of cruising itineraries, charters, and regattas. He ensures that guests enjoy a safe, comfortable, and exceptional experience onboard.\n\nLicences and Qualifications\n\n•\tCaptain 500 GT (Capitaine 500 UMS)\n•\tCaptain 200 Sailing – Unlimited (Capitaine 200 Voile Illimité)\n•\tMedical Level III\n•\tGeneral Radio Operator Certificate (CGO)\n\nLanguages\nEnglish, Spanish, Croatian\n"
    },
